WEBVTT

00:06.047 --> 00:08.049
[opening theme music playing]

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:34.034 --> 00:36.036
[funky pop music playing]

00:40.165 --> 00:44.377
5 YEARS AGO

01:14.908 --> 01:17.368
[man] Thanks for letting me
come see you off.

01:18.745 --> 01:20.288
What else can I give you, honey?

01:22.123 --> 01:23.792
A ceremony would be great.

01:33.051 --> 01:34.344
Will this work for you?

01:37.055 --> 01:38.306
Well, it's what you want.

01:40.725 --> 01:42.185
Please don't kill my mother.

01:44.395 --> 01:45.355
[man chuckles]

01:46.481 --> 01:47.982
Could I pay someone to do it?

01:48.983 --> 01:50.443
Mm, don't think so.

01:51.569 --> 01:52.654
[In-ji laughs]

01:53.738 --> 01:56.449
You think she'll… show up to it?

01:57.367 --> 01:58.827
Uh, nah.

01:59.536 --> 02:02.163
Let's say most people live
to be 80 years old.

02:02.997 --> 02:05.333
Scratch that. We'll live a little longer.

02:05.917 --> 02:08.211
I bet we'll be about a hundred or so,

02:10.004 --> 02:13.007
and you might get tired of it…
living with me.

02:14.300 --> 02:16.761
I'll get rid of you when you're 70,
then it'll be fine.

02:19.055 --> 02:20.557
Forty years. Wow.

02:22.892 --> 02:24.519
What should I do after that?

02:24.602 --> 02:27.939
Well, probably try to live out
the rest of your life with someone else.

02:28.857 --> 02:29.858
With a man.

02:30.900 --> 02:31.943
[chuckles]

02:36.364 --> 02:37.782
Do you think people will…

02:39.075 --> 02:40.618
will be less lonely…

02:43.037 --> 02:43.955
by then?

02:46.166 --> 02:47.333
Did you feel lonely?

02:49.169 --> 02:50.003
Sort of.

02:52.964 --> 02:54.174
But not with you, In-Ji.

02:59.304 --> 03:00.847
I think most of us,

03:02.098 --> 03:03.808
we're either lonely or evil.

03:05.435 --> 03:06.811
And life's taught me that

03:07.812 --> 03:09.022
the lonely ones

03:10.398 --> 03:12.859
always seem to get abandoned
and left in the dust.

03:13.526 --> 03:14.485
[chuckles]

03:17.197 --> 03:18.740
If we do get another life,

03:19.949 --> 03:21.242
let's just bow out.

03:22.952 --> 03:24.245
Let's get left in the dust.

03:26.122 --> 03:28.124
[gentle piano music playing]

03:28.666 --> 03:30.668
I'll always make sure you're not lonely.

03:31.794 --> 03:35.506
I'll take care of you, okay?
You won't have to spend your life hiding.

03:36.674 --> 03:38.301
[both laugh]

03:40.595 --> 03:46.517
THE TRUNK

03:46.601 --> 03:48.603
[gentle piano music continues]

04:06.913 --> 04:08.456
[gentle piano music continues]

04:13.962 --> 04:15.964
[gentle piano music continues]

04:30.687 --> 04:32.981
[gentle piano music continues]

04:57.880 --> 04:59.882
[music fades]

04:59.966 --> 05:00.842
[sighs]

05:00.925 --> 05:02.635
[Hyeon-cheol] I just watched
this documentary

05:02.719 --> 05:04.429
about this tribe called the Mosuo.

05:04.512 --> 05:06.764
In their matriarchal society,
marriage doesn't exist.

05:07.432 --> 05:09.267
They basically treat dating
as the equivalent,

05:09.350 --> 05:11.853
and the parents don't even know
when their kids get married.

05:11.936 --> 05:14.397
When a child is born,
the woman raises the child at her place.

05:14.480 --> 05:16.441
The man raises his older sister's baby.

05:17.483 --> 05:19.485
Their village looked super peaceful too.

05:20.570 --> 05:21.946
What are you getting at?

05:23.114 --> 05:25.408
You don't even watch
the meter in a cab, do you?

05:25.491 --> 05:28.286
You called a taxi at three in the morning
to haul my ass out here.

05:28.369 --> 05:29.871
Come on, at least talk a little.

05:30.371 --> 05:33.291
Or just catch a fish already
so we can make some maeuntang.

05:33.916 --> 05:37.003
Using live bait to capture
another living animal for sport,

05:37.712 --> 05:38.546
it's heartless.

05:40.173 --> 05:41.507
You are heartless.

05:42.258 --> 05:44.093
You know,
I think I'd like to sleep with her.

05:44.177 --> 05:45.094
Who do you mean?

05:47.472 --> 05:48.681
Your new woman?

05:57.273 --> 06:00.401
[woman] The tests indicate
they're not LSD or methamphetamines.

06:00.485 --> 06:03.571
They're mostly sleeping pills
in the zolpidem family, doxepin,

06:03.654 --> 06:06.282
benzodiazepines,
antidepressants, and anxiolytics,

06:06.366 --> 06:07.825
and some melatonin too.

06:08.326 --> 06:10.286
They're all over-the-counter medications,

06:10.370 --> 06:12.914
although it's unusual
for someone to have this many.

06:12.997 --> 06:14.665
Is it unusual to hide them?

06:15.249 --> 06:17.627
If addiction is a factor,
it's quite common.

06:19.003 --> 06:20.963
Well, looks like a rainy day today.

06:21.047 --> 06:23.341
Have a good afternoon. Take care, Ms. Noh.

06:24.634 --> 06:25.510
Okay.

06:27.303 --> 06:28.221
[disconnect tone]

06:34.602 --> 06:36.604
[intriguing music playing]

06:58.167 --> 06:59.335
[knocking at door]

07:00.378 --> 07:01.921
[door opens]

07:04.382 --> 07:05.383
[door closes]

07:06.592 --> 07:08.010
[music fades]

07:08.094 --> 07:09.512
You're working on vacation?

07:14.392 --> 07:18.271
I wanted to give you this the other day,
but the timing wasn't right.

07:19.272 --> 07:20.857
You only wear one, so…

07:28.239 --> 07:29.490
Need a hand with that?

07:32.243 --> 07:34.954
I'm used to this one right now.
I'll wear yours later.

07:41.461 --> 07:43.588
Why were you being so weird
at Jeong-won's?

07:45.798 --> 07:47.508
Acting like the lady of the house.

07:49.302 --> 07:50.136
[chuckles]

07:50.219 --> 07:52.096
I gave it some thought, and

07:53.473 --> 07:56.100
I think it wasn't because of us
or Jeong-won.

07:57.768 --> 07:59.979
You really don't like In-ji, do you?

08:03.900 --> 08:06.027
I lived in that house
for a very long time.

08:06.819 --> 08:09.071
I wasn't acting.
It was just kind of a reflex.

08:09.155 --> 08:12.158
All right. I guess that explains it, then.

08:15.912 --> 08:16.871
Enjoy.

08:24.921 --> 08:25.922
[door closes]

08:26.464 --> 08:27.298
[mouse clicks]

08:32.261 --> 08:34.388
[pensive music playing]

08:45.274 --> 08:47.568
[thunder rumbling]

09:01.374 --> 09:03.376
[pensive music continues]

09:19.141 --> 09:22.603
HAN JEONG-WON

09:45.876 --> 09:47.878
[gunshot echoes]

09:51.674 --> 09:53.467
[ethereal music playing]

09:59.015 --> 10:01.892
[Si-jeong] Ugh, I haven't seen him.
He's still living rent-free in my head.

10:01.976 --> 10:04.186
I thought he'd show up right away
if he got out.

10:06.814 --> 10:07.940
Eom Tae-seong.

10:10.026 --> 10:13.237
So how's this one going?
Is it a nice place?

10:13.321 --> 10:15.031
It's your first time
in a marriage like this.

10:15.114 --> 10:18.117
He's not terminally ill on his deathbed.
That's good.

10:18.200 --> 10:22.038
He's not gay and needs to marry you
because of his parents. [chuckles]

10:22.121 --> 10:25.041
He's not a mental case who's always
trying to commit suicide either.

10:25.666 --> 10:28.628
At least this guy's actually
normal this time.

10:29.670 --> 10:32.298
Good God. It doesn't matter
if these men have issues or not.

10:32.381 --> 10:33.674
It's bad either way.

10:34.634 --> 10:36.385
But this person is kind of troubled.

10:39.597 --> 10:41.307
I mean, he's got addiction issues.

10:44.685 --> 10:46.228
All right, if you say so.

10:47.688 --> 10:50.191
So what are you hoping to get
out of this marriage?

10:52.818 --> 10:55.488
Can you offer him anything
to improve his situation?

10:57.323 --> 10:58.199
Divorce.

11:02.244 --> 11:03.496
A perfect divorce.

11:06.290 --> 11:07.500
[Hyeon-cheol chuckles]

11:07.583 --> 11:09.335
Man, I never thought
I'd live to see the day.

11:09.418 --> 11:12.421
Han Jeong-won moved on
and found himself a different woman.

11:12.922 --> 11:14.674
When you told me you were getting married,

11:14.757 --> 11:17.009
at first, I thought
you were out of your mind.

11:17.593 --> 11:20.680
But then I was just lying around at home,
and I got excited.

11:20.763 --> 11:23.391
Why waste all that effort
looking for a new partner?

11:23.474 --> 11:26.102
Now you get to enjoy married life
with someone who's a perfect match

11:26.185 --> 11:27.645
and no strings attached.

11:27.728 --> 11:29.855
Seriously, lots of men
would be on cloud nine.

11:29.939 --> 11:30.940
Ladies too, actually.

11:31.023 --> 11:32.608
No kids, no annoying in-laws.

11:32.692 --> 11:34.819
Just a peaceful, reliable,
casual marriage.

11:34.902 --> 11:36.195
It's the whole package.

11:37.154 --> 11:39.115
Dude, you into her?

11:39.198 --> 11:40.783
It's not like that.

11:42.034 --> 11:43.744
- It's just…
- What?

11:44.745 --> 11:46.580
Once she moved in, I could sleep.

11:47.581 --> 11:49.542
Sleep and wake up in the morning.

11:49.625 --> 11:52.169
I get so bothered
that she's changing things,

11:52.253 --> 11:54.046
although I don't really know why.

11:56.841 --> 11:58.884
So you wanna do it
with a chick who bothers you?

11:58.968 --> 12:00.761
I think any woman would do, actually.

12:00.845 --> 12:04.014
What are you, 15? You're well over 30.
You should be able to tell.

12:04.098 --> 12:06.434
Look, you need to figure this out.

12:06.517 --> 12:08.310
Do you just need a lady,
or are you in love?

12:08.394 --> 12:09.687
No way. Jesus.

12:12.106 --> 12:13.149
It's not love.

12:13.232 --> 12:16.026
This is why you can't trust people
who think they know everything

12:16.110 --> 12:19.029
after reading one book
or dating one person. You're a moron.

12:19.113 --> 12:20.906
Seo-yeon turned your brain into shit.

12:23.117 --> 12:25.578
[intriguing music playing]

12:39.091 --> 12:40.050
[man] Hey, In-ji.

12:46.056 --> 12:47.349
You shop here too?

12:48.350 --> 12:49.727
What a coincidence.

12:51.187 --> 12:53.189
[intriguing music continues]

12:55.900 --> 12:57.526
[Hyeon-cheol] You need to figure this out.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.779
Do you just need a lady,
or are you in love?

13:01.697 --> 13:02.740
[sighs]

13:11.957 --> 13:13.083
[Jeong-won] Hey, where are…

13:26.472 --> 13:27.681
[man chuckles]

13:27.765 --> 13:29.809
I was happy to run into you in this area.

13:30.559 --> 13:32.102
You're happy about it, why?

13:33.187 --> 13:37.066
I don't have a lot of friends nearby,
ya know? Also… I mean, it's just cool.

13:37.566 --> 13:39.610
We're both taken. Neither of us have exes…

13:40.194 --> 13:43.697
Yeah, I'm wondering if you were just happy
to run into a coworker for a change.

13:45.616 --> 13:46.909
Wait, so you know?

13:47.868 --> 13:50.329
Yes. Well, of course,
Assistant Manager Yoon Ji-o.

13:50.412 --> 13:51.622
[Ji-o chuckles]

13:53.123 --> 13:55.000
I'm sorry. I thought I only knew.

13:56.085 --> 13:58.087
Two husbands in the mix
with two pretty wives.

13:58.796 --> 14:02.216
There's a game like that where the lies
are mixed in with the truth, you know?

14:03.300 --> 14:05.678
Hey, how about… we work together?

14:07.179 --> 14:09.348
This thing with Seo-yeon,
I wanna make it real now.

14:15.271 --> 14:16.605
Does Seo-yeon

14:17.982 --> 14:19.441
take lots of medication?

14:20.359 --> 14:21.735
Sleep aids, for instance?

14:24.989 --> 14:26.323
You mean that as a yes?

14:28.200 --> 14:29.243
[phone buzzing]

14:33.747 --> 14:37.001
[Jeong-won] Would you like
to have dinner together? Maybe a patio?

14:38.502 --> 14:39.753
You can pick the restaurant.

14:42.840 --> 14:43.674
[In-ji] Sure.

14:44.592 --> 14:45.718
Got a date?

14:48.012 --> 14:49.138
I'm gonna head out.

14:50.306 --> 14:51.765
Look, I don't know about you.

14:52.933 --> 14:55.102
I swear I'm on your side, no matter what.

14:58.856 --> 15:00.190
Let's make this work.

15:00.274 --> 15:02.276
[uneasy music playing]

15:12.703 --> 15:14.538
- [music intensifies]
- [grunts]

15:26.133 --> 15:28.135
[indistinct announcement on PA]

15:35.059 --> 15:37.061
[music fades]

15:38.646 --> 15:40.439
Didn't think we'd be eating here.

15:44.068 --> 15:46.570
I thought it'd be satisfying
to eat in front of someone

15:46.654 --> 15:48.280
who can't have a meal like this.

15:50.658 --> 15:51.617
[chuckles]

15:53.452 --> 15:54.536
What's so funny?

15:55.329 --> 15:58.082
I was just wondering why
I really want it, you know?

15:59.416 --> 16:01.627
Do I just need it? Or is there…

16:02.294 --> 16:03.587
is there more to this?

16:07.007 --> 16:08.300
Oh, sorry, never mind.

16:09.385 --> 16:10.302
Dig in.

16:14.974 --> 16:17.351
[In-ji] Aren't you supposed to have
miyeokguk on birthdays?

16:17.434 --> 16:19.103
Why does he like this so much anyway?

16:21.814 --> 16:24.692
People who grew up by the ocean
put rockfish in their miyeokguk

16:24.775 --> 16:25.943
instead of beef.

16:26.527 --> 16:28.696
Once you've had it like that,
it sticks with you forever,

16:28.779 --> 16:30.030
even after you move away.

16:32.616 --> 16:34.034
No matter what you try to do,

16:34.118 --> 16:36.578
you can't recreate
the flavor from your childhood.

16:38.414 --> 16:40.916
He beat her like crazy
because the taste was wrong.

16:50.300 --> 16:52.344
We always had miyeokguk at home.

16:53.846 --> 16:56.265
At first, I thought
it was because my father liked it,

16:56.765 --> 16:58.267
but I found out later

16:59.351 --> 17:01.562
that my mom never even got to

17:01.645 --> 17:04.231
have a bite of the stuff
after she gave birth to me.

17:05.357 --> 17:07.151
[wistful music playing]

17:07.234 --> 17:08.944
Her mother abandoned her as a kid.

17:10.195 --> 17:11.947
It tormented her forever.

17:13.824 --> 17:15.826
[wistful music continues]

17:24.877 --> 17:26.628
[Jeong-won] My father beat her up once,

17:26.712 --> 17:29.590
and after she was taken to the hospital
with broken teeth,

17:31.508 --> 17:34.553
she had made some for herself
without even turning the lights on.

17:35.054 --> 17:37.097
[wistful music continues]

17:37.181 --> 17:38.557
All that over miyeokguk.

17:40.559 --> 17:44.063
Every time she was hurting,
every time she got beaten up,

17:45.314 --> 17:48.108
I don't know if she thought
it was gonna heal her, or, um…

17:49.485 --> 17:52.154
Or who knows? She might've thought
it was a bad omen that…

18:04.833 --> 18:06.794
No one ever made it for her as a child.

18:11.548 --> 18:14.676
With this kind of food,
all I can think of is death.

18:20.057 --> 18:21.642
[music fades]

18:21.725 --> 18:23.435
So, um, what's this?

18:24.770 --> 18:25.813
Protocol.

18:27.940 --> 18:29.775
Comforting each other is allowed.

18:31.693 --> 18:32.528
You're okay.

18:40.911 --> 18:41.995
It's like

18:43.330 --> 18:45.040
me holding your hand on a roller coaster.

18:45.707 --> 18:46.667
[chuckles]

18:53.966 --> 18:57.136
Back in the day,
when Japan occupied Korea,

18:57.219 --> 18:59.096
freedom fighters made these pacts.

18:59.179 --> 19:00.180
You know about this?

19:00.681 --> 19:03.767
They swore to kill each other's fathers
if they were traitors,

19:04.434 --> 19:07.813
all because each of them knew
they couldn't do it to their own father.

19:08.313 --> 19:10.023
Split the hard work, you know?

19:10.816 --> 19:12.484
I take solace knowing

19:13.735 --> 19:15.237
they used to do things like that.

19:21.535 --> 19:22.911
So let's do it.

19:26.206 --> 19:28.000
I can take care of him for you.

19:30.169 --> 19:31.920
You can kill my mother in return.

19:36.466 --> 19:38.468
[intriguing music playing]

19:56.945 --> 19:58.697
[Hyeon-cheol]
I'm guessing my dad's fuming?

19:59.364 --> 20:01.033
Uh, no, I… I'm on my way. Yeah.

20:01.116 --> 20:02.201
I'm going in now.

20:02.284 --> 20:03.243
Yeah, all right.

20:04.077 --> 20:05.245
Oh Hyeon-cheol?

20:05.829 --> 20:06.830
Uh, yes.

20:07.998 --> 20:10.125
I met your wife at the Heritage Lounge.

20:10.209 --> 20:12.878
- She ordered these special rice cakes.
- Oh, great. Thank you.

20:12.961 --> 20:14.087
Big fan too.

20:15.881 --> 20:18.717
Your label's been producing
really good stuff.

20:18.800 --> 20:21.094
Thanks so much.
I… I'm in a bit of a rush, so…

20:22.346 --> 20:23.972
Han Jeong-won is the best.

20:27.517 --> 20:30.604
His work, in particular.
It's extraordinary.

20:32.064 --> 20:33.690
Right. Okay.

20:36.026 --> 20:38.570
- Name is Oh Hyeon-cheol. Thank you.
- [woman] Sure, right this way.

20:42.032 --> 20:43.033
What did you do today?

20:46.954 --> 20:50.499
We're supposed to ask these questions.
We're married. So what did you do?

20:53.293 --> 20:54.169
Fishing.

20:55.462 --> 20:57.464
Do, um, you like fishing?

20:58.215 --> 20:59.049
I don't.

21:00.092 --> 21:00.968
Why not?

21:01.551 --> 21:03.512
All I can think of
is my goldfish when I do it.

21:08.058 --> 21:09.601
What's that look about?

21:13.313 --> 21:16.525
You don't seem to feel all that bad
about grilling them though.

21:17.818 --> 21:19.695
If it bothers you that much, I won't.

21:20.320 --> 21:21.780
Oh my God, you're cruel.

21:25.534 --> 21:26.785
What did you do today?

21:29.621 --> 21:32.291
Hey, it was you that said
we're supposed to ask each other.

21:33.709 --> 21:34.793
Just this and that.

21:35.585 --> 21:39.589
Mostly little things…
that you have to do that no one sees.

21:42.968 --> 21:45.220
I had to run the dryer 'cause it rained.

21:45.304 --> 21:47.597
It's a shame.
I prefer to dry the sheets outside.

21:49.599 --> 21:51.601
[sentimental music playing]

21:52.144 --> 21:53.312
That sounds nice.

21:58.775 --> 22:00.527
You know,
you have such a calming presence.

22:00.610 --> 22:02.904
It's… comforting.

22:02.988 --> 22:04.656
You say these things sometimes.

22:05.574 --> 22:08.410
I don't know if I can even describe it,
but it just…

22:10.370 --> 22:12.080
Like when you do the buttons wrong

22:12.873 --> 22:15.667
on a shirt, and then you redo it
very slowly. It feels right.

22:17.627 --> 22:19.755
Are you not good at buttoning a shirt?

22:20.505 --> 22:22.215
Actually, yeah, when I was little.

22:23.675 --> 22:24.801
I'd do it on purpose too.

22:26.470 --> 22:28.638
When I did it,
my mom's eyes would light up.

22:30.098 --> 22:31.767
She'd go, "You're a mess, hon."

22:35.312 --> 22:39.066
One by one, she'd redo the whole thing.
And for an instant, she was at ease.

22:44.905 --> 22:47.199
You just make people feel comfortable,
I guess.

22:47.699 --> 22:49.493
Why else would I be
telling you these stories?

22:49.576 --> 22:50.869
Not to say that…

22:52.204 --> 22:54.873
that that's the reason
I kissed you the other night.

22:54.956 --> 22:56.958
[sentimental music continues]

23:08.428 --> 23:10.514
[sentimental music continues]

23:16.978 --> 23:18.980
You must've had to do chores as a kid.

23:19.731 --> 23:22.067
Well, my dad didn't like
letting people in the house.

23:22.150 --> 23:24.861
I don't wanna take after him,
but I'm the same way.

23:24.945 --> 23:27.572
I lived like a college kid for ten years.

23:28.365 --> 23:32.077
I didn't buy one piece of furniture.
I just cleaned obsessively.

23:32.160 --> 23:33.203
[music fades]

23:37.374 --> 23:39.668
And whenever I do get
a new furniture piece,

23:39.751 --> 23:42.003
it's like I have to do battle
with it for a while.

23:42.087 --> 23:43.964
Takes me a while to get used to it.

23:46.550 --> 23:47.926
You feel that way about us?

23:51.513 --> 23:53.223
Well, your housework's pretty good.

23:57.519 --> 24:00.730
So about your mother…
Why do you want her to die?

24:01.940 --> 24:05.485
Be good to know if we ever split
the hard work between the two of us.

24:07.195 --> 24:09.114
You don't have to tell me
if you don't want to.

24:10.866 --> 24:11.908
I was married.

24:13.827 --> 24:15.579
She ruined that, of course,

24:17.247 --> 24:18.832
and she got my ex killed.

24:22.752 --> 24:24.754
[pensive music playing]

24:30.135 --> 24:32.137
[pensive music continues]

24:47.819 --> 24:49.821
[pensive music continues]

25:03.084 --> 25:05.295
- [Si-jeong] You killed it?
- [exclaims, gasps]

25:06.254 --> 25:07.839
[Do-dam] Jesus fricking Christ!

25:08.340 --> 25:11.468
What the hell are you doing here so early?
What's going on?

25:11.968 --> 25:14.638
[Si-jeong] You're one to talk.
It's way weirder that you're here now.

25:14.721 --> 25:16.640
[groans] Oh, goddammit.

25:16.723 --> 25:21.102
You try taking care of them, then!
See for yourself how long they survive.

25:21.770 --> 25:23.605
I'm the only reason they lived so long.

25:23.688 --> 25:24.981
Oh, get over yourself.

25:25.065 --> 25:27.859
If you take good care of them,
these damn things outlive dogs.

25:28.360 --> 25:29.569
Keep this to yourself.

25:31.154 --> 25:34.533
She always comes back here
'cause she's attached to this place.

25:35.659 --> 25:36.826
If she heard they died?

25:36.910 --> 25:39.037
Listen to that.
My God, you must care about her.

25:39.120 --> 25:41.915
- Don't even think about blabbing.
- All right, I get it.

25:46.461 --> 25:49.589
The owner, that punk.
He's still alive, isn't he?

25:52.050 --> 25:53.802
He's gonna come back, right?

25:55.262 --> 25:56.137
Mm.

25:57.055 --> 25:58.348
I heard that he's alive.

25:59.140 --> 26:02.435
We all thought he was dead,
but apparently, he's still around.

26:24.624 --> 26:25.959
[In-ji] How have you been?

26:27.085 --> 26:29.254
So polite.
You're not just a South Korean bitch, huh?

26:32.299 --> 26:33.508
Things are going okay.

26:35.343 --> 26:36.595
A meal sound good?

26:52.652 --> 26:54.654
[In-ji] Your husband
still won't agree to it at all?

26:57.741 --> 26:59.868
What about keeping the next child?

27:03.246 --> 27:05.665
The OBGYN said I won't have other kids.

27:06.666 --> 27:08.585
I guess I was born with a weak uterus.

27:10.128 --> 27:12.631
I've lost contact
with my youngest sibling.

27:12.714 --> 27:14.883
I didn't even see her corpse in my dreams.

27:15.800 --> 27:16.801
I'm sure she's dead.

27:18.261 --> 27:19.888
Now I'm really alone, and, uh…

27:20.972 --> 27:22.474
and all I have is this baby.

27:26.311 --> 27:27.646
And I want it bad.

27:28.355 --> 27:29.731
[pensive music playing]

27:30.982 --> 27:33.276
I'm sure NM won't take that lying down.

27:35.487 --> 27:37.530
If you gave birth to a child
the husband doesn't want,

27:37.614 --> 27:39.366
the company
would have to pay a lot to fix it.

27:41.242 --> 27:42.661
One other thing before…

27:50.168 --> 27:52.003
[In-yeong] Those are the brokers
that were updating me.

27:52.087 --> 27:53.421
Apparently, he's still over there.

27:53.505 --> 27:57.550
He worked for a trading organization
that exchanges goods internationally.

27:57.634 --> 28:00.011
And now he's working as a tour guide,
I think.

28:00.804 --> 28:02.138
He sells fishbowls too.

28:03.932 --> 28:04.933
Fishbowls.

28:05.433 --> 28:06.309
It's ridiculous.

28:07.185 --> 28:10.480
I get the feeling…
he's going to try to return here someday,

28:10.563 --> 28:11.398
but I

28:12.607 --> 28:14.567
don't know if he's coming back to you,
Ms. Noh.

28:22.826 --> 28:24.327
So where are you headed?

28:25.453 --> 28:26.579
Mm…

28:28.081 --> 28:29.165
Uh, home.

28:48.977 --> 28:50.311
[Jeong-won] Wanna go see a movie?

29:00.864 --> 29:01.781
It's cool here, huh?

29:02.949 --> 29:04.909
Seo-yeon did good work, I think.

29:05.910 --> 29:07.454
Hey, how was your dad's birthday?

29:07.537 --> 29:09.122
Oh, the rice cakes saved it.

29:10.123 --> 29:12.459
Actually, the guy from the rice cake place
knows you.

29:12.542 --> 29:13.376
Who?

29:13.460 --> 29:15.628
Apparently, he listens to all our records.

29:15.712 --> 29:18.840
He's a fan. Never thought
I'd run into a Han Jeong-won fan.

29:18.923 --> 29:19.758
[phone buzzing]

29:22.302 --> 29:23.845
[In-ji] Yeah, sure.

29:23.928 --> 29:25.930
[footsteps approaching]

29:28.141 --> 29:29.350
[Hyeon-cheol] Oh, hi, Seo-yeon.

29:29.893 --> 29:31.311
I'll take off.

29:31.394 --> 29:34.063
Why are you here?
For the remodeling project?

29:35.440 --> 29:37.150
Did you just get some good news
or something?

29:45.784 --> 29:46.701
Thank you.

29:47.285 --> 29:49.746
I'm free right now.
Wanna grab a quick bite?

29:52.415 --> 29:54.125
It's okay if you're too busy.

29:54.209 --> 29:56.419
Sorry. I would.
I just can't miss this thing.

29:57.754 --> 29:59.923
If we did it tomorrow,
I could find an opening for you.

30:00.799 --> 30:02.091
All right. Let's do that.

30:02.801 --> 30:04.135
Okay, sounds good, then.

30:11.267 --> 30:12.602
[movie monster snarling]

30:12.685 --> 30:14.771
I'm sorry, but I got the tickets late.

30:14.854 --> 30:16.272
This was the only option.

30:17.232 --> 30:18.858
I actually like this genre.

30:21.152 --> 30:22.904
[screaming]

30:27.075 --> 30:28.409
[screaming continues]

30:30.578 --> 30:32.580
[tense movie music playing]

30:43.591 --> 30:45.593
[screaming continues]

30:48.930 --> 30:51.349
[melodic acoustic guitar music playing]

30:51.432 --> 30:52.976
Why aren't you watching?

30:56.938 --> 30:58.189
Because it's scary.

30:59.941 --> 31:01.901
I get freaked out at these movies.

31:07.407 --> 31:08.575
[In-ji chuckles]

31:33.892 --> 31:35.226
You gonna be okay?

31:38.605 --> 31:40.148
[laughs]

31:48.323 --> 31:51.159
[female voice] The number you have dialed
is not available. At the tone--

31:51.242 --> 31:53.953
HAN JEONG-WON

31:54.996 --> 31:56.289
[phone line ringing]

31:57.332 --> 31:59.751
[female voice] The number you have dialed
is not available.

32:02.003 --> 32:03.922
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

32:21.230 --> 32:23.107
You don't get scared at these movies?

32:24.525 --> 32:25.485
Yeah, I do.

32:27.904 --> 32:29.322
You didn't seem scared.

32:31.491 --> 32:34.243
Well, most of the time,
I find horror movies reassuring.

32:34.786 --> 32:36.412
It's always a bit of a relief

32:37.121 --> 32:39.123
when you compare your life
to what's on-screen.

32:39.207 --> 32:40.959
It's easy to see how lucky you are.

32:42.418 --> 32:44.671
From what I've heard,
that's why people love horror.

32:47.340 --> 32:49.425
Do you feel like
you need that relief a lot?

32:51.678 --> 32:52.679
I guess so.

32:55.306 --> 32:56.641
That makes two of us.

33:01.312 --> 33:03.523
I was really glad
you asked me out tonight.

33:04.023 --> 33:05.441
I liked the movie a lot too.

33:12.198 --> 33:14.659
I guess you needed
to feel some relief, In-ji.

33:17.078 --> 33:18.204
Guess so.

33:20.248 --> 33:21.290
Do you know why?

33:23.459 --> 33:25.586
My mother tried to kill this guy, and I'm

33:27.088 --> 33:28.381
supposed to

33:29.757 --> 33:30.758
meet the guy soon.

33:30.842 --> 33:32.468
So, yeah, I think that's it.

33:41.519 --> 33:42.687
I'm not sure

33:44.230 --> 33:45.857
it's the right moment, but…

33:52.363 --> 33:54.449
Well, I think I'd like to sleep with you.

33:59.037 --> 34:00.872
I wish I could be a bit more subtle.

34:01.831 --> 34:03.624
I just wanna be honest, that's all.

34:04.167 --> 34:06.544
[melodic piano music playing]

34:06.627 --> 34:08.504
The reason I'm bringing it up now…

34:10.882 --> 34:14.385
is… is because I'm worried
nothing will come of it if I wait.

34:15.595 --> 34:19.098
I always think of
subtracting things from my life.

34:19.182 --> 34:20.683
I just subtract.

34:21.684 --> 34:23.895
Now I have a simple life,
and I just can't…

34:25.938 --> 34:27.523
can't figure out how you fit.

34:31.110 --> 34:33.196
I dunno if I wanna sleep with you 'cause…

34:36.032 --> 34:38.826
just 'cause you're a woman,
or if it's more than that.

34:40.745 --> 34:41.829
I'm hoping…

34:44.499 --> 34:47.043
this is easy,
and it's just because you're a woman.

34:47.126 --> 34:49.962
♪ I can pull you out of shadows ♪

34:50.046 --> 34:53.466
♪ Just hold my hand, and we'll be fine ♪

34:54.342 --> 34:55.760
♪ Turn around… ♪

34:55.843 --> 34:57.095
I'll consider that.

34:57.762 --> 35:01.682
♪ Baby, I'll be your savior ♪

35:06.521 --> 35:08.523
♪ What if we die? ♪

35:09.107 --> 35:14.195
♪ We cannot be happy
If there's nothing to lose ♪

35:16.697 --> 35:18.699
♪ What if we try ♪

35:19.200 --> 35:20.409
♪ To stay alive? ♪

35:20.493 --> 35:24.122
♪ Will we ever be free from the past… ♪

35:24.747 --> 35:27.708
WIFE

35:29.502 --> 35:32.880
♪ What do we live for? ♪

35:34.632 --> 35:37.301
♪ What do we live for? ♪

35:37.885 --> 35:39.595
♪ Mm-mm-mm ♪

35:39.679 --> 35:43.224
♪ So what do we live for? ♪

35:48.271 --> 35:50.148
[music fades]

35:50.231 --> 35:51.357
Where's the whiskey?

36:09.959 --> 36:11.294
Take it slow, will ya?

36:15.214 --> 36:16.382
I'll take one more.

36:16.883 --> 36:17.717
Get it yourself.

36:17.800 --> 36:20.052
- I poured the first one, didn't I?
- You do it!

36:25.892 --> 36:29.478
There's supposed to be one person
in my life I have total control over.

36:30.396 --> 36:31.480
And that's you.

36:36.402 --> 36:38.321
So that's it? You really don't care

36:39.322 --> 36:41.199
who I am or what I used to do before?

36:41.282 --> 36:43.534
And why the hell would I wanna know that?

36:44.160 --> 36:46.370
You can't control me
because I like you, and this works.

36:48.623 --> 36:49.498
That's wrong.

36:50.458 --> 36:51.876
I own you right now.

36:53.211 --> 36:54.128
For a year.

36:59.508 --> 37:00.801
[glass clatters]

37:00.885 --> 37:01.969
[whiskey pouring]

37:04.764 --> 37:06.891
Stop the boozing.
You look pathetic enough.

37:15.691 --> 37:17.693
[electronic music playing]

37:23.407 --> 37:24.242
Sir.

37:25.534 --> 37:26.786
We ID'd the body.

37:27.787 --> 37:28.663
Eom Tae-seong?

37:28.746 --> 37:31.499
[man 1] That's right, Eom Tae-seong.
Thirty-six-year-old male.

37:31.582 --> 37:34.168
History of mental illness.
Even committed for treatment.

37:34.961 --> 37:38.381
Uh, he died from a chest wound.
He had a wound on his leg too.

37:41.926 --> 37:42.760
[sighs]

37:44.804 --> 37:46.180
[Do-dam sighs] Shit.

37:46.264 --> 37:47.515
[electronic music continues]

37:47.598 --> 37:49.809
Do I need to get a whole new tank of fish?

37:51.435 --> 37:52.895
They're not doing so hot.

38:07.118 --> 38:08.286
[device beeps]

38:09.495 --> 38:10.621
[door closes]

38:10.705 --> 38:11.998
[keypad beeping]

38:12.081 --> 38:13.708
[door lock clicks, beeps]

38:17.378 --> 38:18.462
[door closes]

38:21.924 --> 38:23.926
[uneasy music playing]

39:13.851 --> 39:16.479
[man 2] How was he related
to the owner of the trunk though?

39:17.063 --> 39:19.565
That's the thing. I couldn't
find a connection between the two.

39:19.648 --> 39:22.109
[sighs] So it's just larceny?

39:22.735 --> 39:24.236
That's what it looks like right now.

39:24.320 --> 39:27.823
[scoffs] I don't get why
the robber hops on a boat after midnight.

39:27.907 --> 39:30.951
Why didn't he take a taxi or a bus?
What's the deal?

39:31.035 --> 39:32.661
Maybe he was avoiding the CCTVs.

39:32.745 --> 39:35.331
Ugh, you're the one who told me
that most of the wires were cut.

39:35.414 --> 39:37.666
Yeah, well,
the dead guy might not have known.

39:38.959 --> 39:41.379
Were there reports of anyone
in the area using a boat?

39:41.462 --> 39:43.297
Engine sounds, wakes, anything?

39:43.381 --> 39:45.758
We've been questioning lots of folks. No.

39:45.841 --> 39:47.259
[man 2 sighs]

39:47.343 --> 39:50.221
Oh, and, um,
our dead guy had quite the rap sheet.

39:51.263 --> 39:53.349
Oh really? So anything recent?

39:54.058 --> 39:54.975
Yeah, stalking.

39:55.518 --> 39:59.230
And he was a repeat offender, actually.
His sentence was commuted at trial.

39:59.313 --> 40:02.024
Before that, he was fined for stalking.
Even did some time.

40:02.108 --> 40:03.359
It was his seventh offense.

40:03.442 --> 40:04.944
Who'd he stalk?

40:10.074 --> 40:11.367
- Huh?
- Who is it?

40:11.450 --> 40:13.202
Come on, just spit it out already.

40:13.869 --> 40:16.122
Han Jeong-won's wife, what's that about?

40:16.205 --> 40:17.623
What's this name doing here?

40:18.124 --> 40:19.333
Is it Lee Seo-yeon?

40:19.417 --> 40:21.419
No, not his ex-wife.
The one he married after her.

40:21.502 --> 40:24.171
And I'm pretty sure it was temporary.
Noh In-ji.

40:25.297 --> 40:28.426
Reach out to Noh In-ji.
And get me Han Jeong-won's address too.

40:30.845 --> 40:33.389
[electronic music playing]

40:46.735 --> 40:47.570
[door closes]

40:49.280 --> 40:50.948
[electronic music continues]

41:08.883 --> 41:10.009
[music fades]

41:18.392 --> 41:21.228
- A Heritage Lounge gathering?
- Mm-hmm.

41:23.022 --> 41:24.106
Okay, have fun.

41:32.364 --> 41:34.533
I only let my guard down with you.

41:34.617 --> 41:37.995
The truth is, there's nowhere else
I… can feel vulnerable.

41:46.462 --> 41:47.963
Seriously, enjoy.

41:50.841 --> 41:51.842
Just try not to argue.

41:53.886 --> 41:55.221
And be careful in traffic.

41:58.057 --> 41:59.099
See you soon.

42:19.578 --> 42:21.789
[woman 1] I just got
this lovely mugwort tea,

42:21.872 --> 42:23.624
and I wanted to show it off.

42:27.378 --> 42:28.587
[Yoon-a] Mmm!

42:28.671 --> 42:30.673
Whoa, it's so good! Don't you think?

42:31.173 --> 42:32.299
It sure is.

42:33.342 --> 42:35.511
I heard you had dinner at Jeong-won's.

42:36.845 --> 42:37.972
Yes.

42:38.055 --> 42:41.433
You're telling me you had an ex-couple
and their new spouses in the same room?

42:41.934 --> 42:42.810
Oh shoot.

42:42.893 --> 42:45.437
I wish you would've called us, too,
since it was a special…

42:49.275 --> 42:51.360
We just had a nice meal,
and then we called it a night.

42:51.443 --> 42:53.362
It's so nice you're getting along.

42:55.489 --> 42:57.741
Oh, is it true we're gonna have
another guest today?

42:58.492 --> 43:00.703
I asked Noh In-ji to join.

43:00.786 --> 43:02.288
I was supposed to meet her later,

43:02.371 --> 43:04.790
but something came up,
and I had to reschedule.

43:05.332 --> 43:07.585
You've already met,
so I figured it would be fine now.

43:08.460 --> 43:11.547
But I can always change things
if you're uncomfortable.

43:11.630 --> 43:13.299
No, that sounds good.

43:14.008 --> 43:15.759
You're okay with this, I'm sure.

43:15.843 --> 43:17.928
I mean,
you both had a meal together already.

43:18.679 --> 43:19.680
[chuckles wryly]

43:22.057 --> 43:24.059
[pensive music playing]

43:39.366 --> 43:42.202
[woman 2] Excuse me.
Your guest is here, ma'am.

43:48.125 --> 43:49.293
[woman 1] Ah, you're here.

43:52.880 --> 43:53.714
Hello there.

43:53.797 --> 43:56.300
Sorry about this.
They were already scheduled.

43:56.842 --> 43:59.720
I thought it would be so nice
to have you all here.

44:00.387 --> 44:01.430
Is that okay?

44:04.558 --> 44:05.392
Yes.

44:09.813 --> 44:11.815
[pensive music continues]

44:20.199 --> 44:22.951
[woman 1] There we are.
Let's just enjoy some tea.

44:23.535 --> 44:25.829
It's been a while, hasn't it, In-ji?
I'm Kang Yoon-a.

44:26.789 --> 44:28.290
Of course, that's right.

44:31.835 --> 44:33.212
[music fades]

44:33.295 --> 44:34.672
So how are you doing?

44:35.881 --> 44:39.009
I'm sorry I never reached out
after dinner. Is Jeong-won…

44:43.472 --> 44:45.349
Is your husband doing okay?

44:46.642 --> 44:47.476
He is.

44:47.559 --> 44:49.770
Your husband's been doing well too,
I take it?

44:56.402 --> 44:58.946
Uh, were you with Jeong-won yesterday?

44:59.738 --> 45:02.908
I was trying to reach him about
soundproofing for his recording studio.

45:02.991 --> 45:04.076
He wasn't picking up.

45:04.618 --> 45:08.831
He asked for a specific brand, but, uh,
the names are all similar, and I forgot.

45:09.415 --> 45:11.750
Right. The two of us decided
to go see a movie.

45:12.835 --> 45:14.628
I'm sure that he turned his phone off.

45:16.046 --> 45:16.922
Uh-huh.

45:25.514 --> 45:27.391
What kind of tea do you like, In-ji?

45:27.474 --> 45:29.601
We're having some mugwort that I just got.

45:29.685 --> 45:31.311
There are other options though.

45:32.563 --> 45:33.939
Let's try that raspberry tea.

45:34.773 --> 45:37.192
I had it on my last visit,
and it was just wonderful.

45:38.777 --> 45:40.612
I think In-ji would love it too, right?

45:41.113 --> 45:43.240
[pensive music resumes]

45:44.241 --> 45:45.200
Is that okay?

45:47.703 --> 45:48.787
Yes.

46:07.055 --> 46:08.182
How is it?

46:10.893 --> 46:13.479
I worried you wouldn't like it
because I recommended it.

46:14.938 --> 46:15.898
It's great.

46:15.981 --> 46:17.733
[music fades]

46:17.816 --> 46:19.151
Berries are so great.

46:25.699 --> 46:27.826
What do beets do for you?
Are they healthy?

46:27.910 --> 46:29.369
[pensive music playing]

46:29.453 --> 46:32.372
Yeah, I heard
beets are actually really healthy.

46:33.791 --> 46:35.959
I drink them in the morning.
They're energizing.

46:36.543 --> 46:37.503
Oh.

46:39.379 --> 46:41.465
You see, I have always wondered…

46:44.259 --> 46:46.136
how anyone can stomach those things.

46:58.649 --> 46:59.942
Why don't we have Ms. Noh join us

47:00.025 --> 47:02.277
for the Heritage Lounge gatherings
as well, ma'am?

47:03.070 --> 47:04.696
[woman 1] Oh, I would love that.

47:04.780 --> 47:06.532
He's her husband, after all.

47:09.368 --> 47:10.953
[chuckles] Of course.

47:14.540 --> 47:18.085
I'm fine with it, you know?
If you were worried I wouldn't be.

47:22.214 --> 47:23.048
Great.

47:24.675 --> 47:25.884
I wasn't concerned.

47:37.980 --> 47:39.231
So where's your car?

47:39.898 --> 47:41.692
A public parking lot over there.

47:42.526 --> 47:45.404
There are better spaces on the other side.
You should go there next time.

47:46.071 --> 47:47.197
How about you, Yoon-a?

47:47.865 --> 47:50.951
Oh, I've got another class this afternoon
because the kids are coming home later.

47:51.869 --> 47:54.872
Well… it was a pleasure to see you.

47:56.123 --> 47:57.165
Right.

47:57.249 --> 47:59.251
[pensive music playing]

48:12.681 --> 48:14.266
[groans] Oh God.

48:15.684 --> 48:16.768
I'm exhausted.

48:16.852 --> 48:18.854
[pensive music continues]

48:23.567 --> 48:25.319
[uneasy music playing]

48:25.402 --> 48:27.070
- [engine roars]
- [tires squeal]

48:28.739 --> 48:30.115
[crashing]

48:31.450 --> 48:33.160
[panting]

48:36.121 --> 48:37.080
[sighs]

48:52.679 --> 48:55.015
[panting]

48:58.936 --> 49:02.105
Are you all right?
Sorry, a cat ran right into the street.

49:08.904 --> 49:10.572
We're gonna need to tow your car.

49:14.409 --> 49:15.577
[music stops]

49:18.622 --> 49:21.500
I've never been in an accident,
even when I learned to drive.

49:22.000 --> 49:24.002
It's all right though.
We'll get your car fixed.

49:25.754 --> 49:27.631
We should tell Jeong-won.
He'll take care of it.

49:27.714 --> 49:31.259
I know. I'd still rather do it.
I hit the car, right?

49:31.843 --> 49:33.637
Why don't we just
keep this between us, huh?

49:34.721 --> 49:35.722
But why would we?

49:40.394 --> 49:42.062
You uncomfortable with secrets?

49:43.188 --> 49:45.315
Well, it just seems unnecessary
to me, I guess.

49:45.399 --> 49:46.566
[laughs]

49:48.360 --> 49:49.861
I guess you're not a fan of secrets.

49:50.696 --> 49:53.448
Sure, okay. What is the point
of hiding stuff like this?

49:55.075 --> 49:58.578
Aren't there some things that
are better off not being revealed at all?

50:00.664 --> 50:04.126
Like, for example,
the fact that you and Jeong-won are…

50:05.252 --> 50:07.629
are in a temporary situation,
and that's all.

50:12.884 --> 50:14.219
You don't seem shocked.

50:15.637 --> 50:18.140
Well, the company just told me
that the ex-wife requested it.

50:19.016 --> 50:20.308
That's not all though.

50:20.809 --> 50:23.729
The thing is,
I… I actually chose you, In-ji.

50:23.812 --> 50:24.688
Did you know?

50:25.230 --> 50:27.232
[unsettling music playing]

50:28.608 --> 50:31.778
They told me there's absolutely no way
you guys would match,

50:31.862 --> 50:33.155
so I thought it was over.

50:34.406 --> 50:37.284
Your decision to take the job
made my life a lot more fun.

50:47.002 --> 50:49.337
Is that true?
Did you really choose me, Seo-yeon?

50:51.131 --> 50:52.132
Yes.

50:53.383 --> 50:55.969
How could you do all this
just to hurt Jeong-won more?

51:01.558 --> 51:03.101
[commentator on TV] …from the goal kick.

51:03.894 --> 51:05.979
Can they get it into that center forward?

51:06.063 --> 51:08.440
Can it go quicker
than it's been going in all game?

51:08.523 --> 51:11.193
[In-ji] How could you do all this
just to hurt Jeong-won more?

51:12.527 --> 51:14.780
[Seo-yeon] You know the fable
of the scorpion and the frog?

51:14.863 --> 51:16.865
After stinging the frog
that saved its life,

51:16.948 --> 51:18.784
the scorpion said it had no choice.

51:18.867 --> 51:20.660
It was in its nature to sting.

51:21.953 --> 51:24.623
Most of us
only see things from our point of view.

51:27.876 --> 51:30.921
In-ji, I think…
you seem like a diligent wife.

51:31.505 --> 51:34.424
You cook breakfast for him
and all this elaborate seafood.

51:34.508 --> 51:38.470
I appreciate you providing like this.
I would never be able to make that work.

51:39.471 --> 51:41.890
Have fun… at least for a year.

51:41.973 --> 51:46.019
I do wanna chasten Jeong-won,
but he should get to enjoy it.

51:49.356 --> 51:51.733
[Seo-yeon] What do beets do for you?
Are they healthy?

51:51.817 --> 51:54.111
[tense music playing]

51:55.612 --> 51:58.865
The thing is, I actually chose you, In-ji,
just so you know.

52:06.790 --> 52:08.416
[tense music swells]

52:08.500 --> 52:10.252
- [gasps]
- [music fades]

52:11.419 --> 52:13.213
[panting]

52:18.844 --> 52:21.054
[breathing heavily]

52:27.102 --> 52:29.104
[uneasy music playing]

53:11.313 --> 53:13.023
[music fades]

53:24.618 --> 53:25.702
You awake?

53:27.787 --> 53:29.998
You seemed uncomfortable, so I moved you.

53:34.044 --> 53:35.837
You still subtracting, Jeong-won?

53:35.921 --> 53:36.963
[Jeong-won sighs]

53:37.547 --> 53:38.673
I really don't know.

53:40.842 --> 53:43.637
Forget about that.
It was just a bunch of nonsense.

53:51.686 --> 53:52.979
I'll consider that.

54:21.883 --> 54:23.885
[romantic music playing]

54:46.783 --> 54:48.785
[both breathing heavily]

55:24.821 --> 55:26.823
[romantic music continues]

57:19.519 --> 57:21.521
[music fades]
